    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using `.loc` helps because it explicitly targets the data to modify, but it does not change how pandas determines if the selection is a view or a copy when applied to filtered results. To resolve the warning and ensure you are working on a copy, you should assign a proper copy of the dataframe to a variable before performing operations on it.\n```python\ndf_copy = df.copy()\ndf_copy.loc[df_copy['age'] > 30, 'new_col'] = 'old'\n```\nThis approach guarantees that you are modifying an independent object, preventing unintended data modifications to the original dataframe, even if the warning message itself is sometimes suppressed by newer pandas versions.",
